WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.938
This is the heart of the
chapter, in two parts.

2
00:00:02.938 --> 00:00:05.188
Learn's ordering is kept as the model.

3
00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:09.476
But the on-premises table has no column
for the delegated managed service

4
00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:13.413
account at all, so the best target on
a new domain never comes out of it.

5
00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.539
It admits a plain user
account in every situation,

6
00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:18.750
so it never tells you to move off one.

7
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.288
It has no way to say retire,

8
00:00:20.288 --> 00:00:24.388
so an orphaned or disabled account
would just get a new account type.

9
00:00:24.388 --> 00:00:28.400
And it decides on facts like server
counts that no register holds.

10
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.110
The code fills each gap,
and a test pins every row.
